extends RefCounted
## Hero definitions. Everything the game, the HUD and the generic hero AI need to know about a hero
## lives here as data; the hero-specific behaviour lives in its kit script (kit_*.gd).
##
## Adding a hero = one entry here + one kit script + art. No AI code changes are needed:
## hero_ai.gd reads each skill's "ai" block (roles / aim / thresholds) and the kit's est_damage().
##
## skill "type":  passive | no_target | point | unit | unit_or_point
## skill "ind":   targeting indicator drawn while aiming: line | blink | circle | dash | unit | self
## skill "ai":
##   roles  : nuke, disable, gap_close, escape, aoe, buff_attack, ult   (what the skill is good for)
##   aim    : target (point at the target), unit (cast on the target), cluster (best AoE point), self
##   radius : AoE radius used for cluster scoring
##   min_heroes / min_creeps : how many foes an AoE should catch before it is worth casting
##   prefer_status : status on the target that makes the skill much better (combo hint, e.g. "charged")
##   setup_status  : status this skill applies (lets the AI open a combo with it)

## all heroes use the 3C control scheme (WASD + mouse aim, right-click signature skill, "c3": true).
## Order = the hero grid: one row per role (tank / carry / support).
